WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.120
If your child receives benefits like SSI or Medicaid,

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.835
a direct inheritance can put those benefits

3
00:00:08.835 --> 00:00:10.600
at risk.

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.145
These programs limit the money a person can hold.

5
00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:19.943
For SSI, that is two thousand dollars for one person.

6
00:00:19.943 --> 00:00:24.100
An inheritance can push someone past it.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:29.033
A special needs trust holds the inheritance instead,

8
00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:33.100
and a trustee spends it on extras.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.270
Think therapies, travel,

10
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.102
a phone, activities.

11
00:00:37.102 --> 00:00:39.022
It supplements benefits.

12
00:00:39.022 --> 00:00:41.600
It doesn't replace them.

13
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.030
There are different types,

14
00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.023
depending on whose money funds it.

15
00:00:47.023 --> 00:00:48.552
The rules differ,

16
00:00:48.552 --> 00:00:52.600
including what happens to leftover funds.

17
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:56.517
Many families also write a letter of intent,

18
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:59.027
describing routines, doctors,

19
00:00:59.027 --> 00:01:02.600
and what makes their child happy.

20
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.571
Every situation is different.

21
00:01:05.571 --> 00:01:09.686
Our guide can help you prepare for a conversation

22
00:01:09.686 --> 00:01:12.100
with an attorney.
